# race-timeattack-mc: TIME ATTACK on JACK 1 MUTE CITY (one machine, no ghost on a fresh save), for
# the n60ships GP-vs-TT receipts ([ships] census md=14, [lsplit] one-racer logic) and the NRR
# categories' one-machine path. Menu walk: SELECT MODE grid (TIME ATTACK = top row, second
# column), then A through the course / machine / settings screens as the practice replay does.
# A ghost needs a finished 3-lap run in the same session (racer.c: D_800F5DEA writes gGhosts on
# a finished time attack; Race_Init loads gGhostRacers from them on the retry), which an
# open-loop script cannot drive; see docs/research/native/n60ships-progress.md.
# SHOT PLACEMENT IS NOT AUTHORED HERE (NEXT.md B15/B43): derive it with tools/dev/covsched.py.
build native/n60ships
seed1 0x1234abcd
seed2 0x0fedcba9
pins renderthread=0 rival_detail_auto=0 stereo=0 fh_every=0
at 400
press START 15 0
at 700
press RIGHT 12 0
at 1000
press A 15 0
at 1300
press A 15 0
at 1600
press A 15 0
at 1900
press A 15 0
at 2200
press A 15 0
at 2500
press A 15 0
at 2800
press A 15 0
at 3100
press A 15 0
at 3400
press A 15 0
at 3700
press A 15 0
# --- race: full throttle down the start straight, then coast (an open-loop steer leaves the
# course within ~15 s and retires the machine; coasting keeps the one machine on track and
# active for the rest of the recording) ---
at 3900
hold A 420
hold B 60
len 6000
